  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>5a8e69feeb6c98563ee2809a457b9cdd</srcmd5>
    <version>0.180.0</version>
    <time>1793725180</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- updated to 0.180.0 (0.18)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Statistics-CaseResampling/Changes
  0.18  Sun Oct 11 10:00:00 2026
    - Fix wild stack pointer deallocation (SIGABRT free() invalid pointer)
      when passing empty arrays to resampling/statistical functions (SCR-01).
    - Prevent use-after-free and double-free under ithreads by adding CLONE
      and CLONE_SKIP handlers for the PRNG state (SCR-02).
    - Fix out-of-bounds indexing in first_quartile and third_quartile for
      small samples (SCR-03).
    - Clamp confidence limit indices to valid sample bounds on extreme
      confidence levels (SCR-04).
    - Validate resample run counts (runs &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; runs &lt;= 100000000) (SCR-05).
    - Fix memory leak on invalid kth selection in select_kth (SCR-06).
    - Guard sample and population standard deviation calculations against
      division by zero on small sample sizes (SCR-07).
    - Use Perl memory allocator (Newx/Safefree) consistently in
      median_absolute_deviation (SCR-08).
    - Harden U32ArrayPtr buffer allocation and size validation (SCR-09).
    - Add comprehensive regression test suite in t/03_security.t.
    - Update author contact details to cpan@steffen-mueller.net.</comment>
    <requestid>1394671</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
